# ALLOWLIST.md's keccak256 is committed on chain, so its bytes are load-bearing:
# a checkout that rewrote its line endings would hash to something that does not
# match the commitment, and the reader would rightly conclude the rules changed.
# Pin it to LF so every clone holds the bytes the hash was taken over.
ALLOWLIST.md text eol=lf
ALLOWLIST.hash text eol=lf
